    "Did you ever use AI to support your math learning in the last year? If yes, how was your experience?": "No, but I’ve seen tools like Wolfram Alpha or basic calculators help others visualize equations. If I were to try, I’d likely use it for quick checks—like verifying a derivative step—rather than relying on it entirely. My self-employment means I often learn independently, so AI would be more of an assistant than a crutch.",
